WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.843
Hello, and welcome to week three: add decimals in columns.

2
00:00:04.843 --> 00:00:08.163
By the end, you will be able to add amounts of money in columns,

3
00:00:08.163 --> 00:00:10.590
lining up the decimal points.

4
00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:12.328
Let's start.

5
00:00:13.478 --> 00:00:18.877
Make one pound twenty-four and two pounds fifty-three with coins, one under the other.

6
00:00:18.877 --> 00:00:25.169
Put them together: the one pence coins, then the ten pence coins, then the one pound coins.

7
00:00:25.169 --> 00:00:28.596
Pause the video and have a go.

8
00:00:37.246 --> 00:00:43.957
Pounds go under pounds, ten pence coins under ten pence coins and one pence coins under one pence coins.

9
00:00:43.957 --> 00:00:47.126
Four pence and three pence make seven pence.

10
00:00:47.126 --> 00:00:51.317
Two ten pence and five ten pence make seven ten pence.

11
00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:54.962
One pound and two pounds make three pounds.

12
00:00:54.962 --> 00:00:58.743
Altogether three pounds seventy-seven.

13
00:01:00.643 --> 00:01:04.579
Now one pound thirty-six plus two pounds twenty-seven.

14
00:01:04.579 --> 00:01:08.015
Put the one pence coins together: thirteen of them.

15
00:01:08.015 --> 00:01:11.823
Exchange ten one pence coins for one ten pence coin.

16
00:01:11.823 --> 00:01:14.786
Pause the video and have a go.

17
00:01:23.436 --> 00:01:27.058
Six pence and seven pence make thirteen pence.

18
00:01:27.058 --> 00:01:29.996
Ten one pence coins make ten pence,

19
00:01:29.996 --> 00:01:35.801
so I exchange them for one ten pence coin and write a small one under the ten pence column.

20
00:01:35.801 --> 00:01:37.565
Three pence is left.

21
00:01:37.565 --> 00:01:42.917
Then the ten pence coins: three, two and the new one make six.

22
00:01:42.917 --> 00:01:46.760
One pound and two pounds make three pounds.

23
00:01:46.760 --> 00:01:50.646
Altogether three pounds sixty-three.

24
00:01:52.546 --> 00:01:57.202
Now two pounds fifty-two plus one pound sixty-four.

25
00:01:57.202 --> 00:02:00.627
This time the ten pence coins make ten or more.

26
00:02:00.627 --> 00:02:05.294
Exchange ten ten pence coins for one one pound coin.

27
00:02:05.294 --> 00:02:08.732
Pause the video and have a go.

28
00:02:17.382 --> 00:02:20.389
Two pence and four pence make six pence.

29
00:02:20.389 --> 00:02:24.580
Five ten pence and six ten pence make eleven ten pence.

30
00:02:24.580 --> 00:02:27.169
Ten ten pence coins make one pound,

31
00:02:27.169 --> 00:02:32.521
so I exchange them for a one pound coin and write a small one under the pounds.

32
00:02:32.521 --> 00:02:34.669
One ten pence is left.

33
00:02:34.669 --> 00:02:40.021
Then the pounds: two, one and the new one make four.

34
00:02:40.021 --> 00:02:44.267
Altogether four pounds sixteen.

35
00:02:46.167 --> 00:02:48.501
Plain decimals work the same way.

36
00:02:48.501 --> 00:02:54.259
One point seven plus zero point five six is like one pound seventy plus fifty-six pence:

37
00:02:54.259 --> 00:02:57.731
write the zero, so the decimal points are in a line.

38
00:02:57.731 --> 00:03:01.146
Pause the video and have a go.

39
00:03:09.796 --> 00:03:16.054
One point seven has no hundredths, so I write one point seven zero, like one pound seventy.

40
00:03:16.054 --> 00:03:18.295
Now the decimal points are in a line.

41
00:03:18.295 --> 00:03:21.301
Zero and six make six.

42
00:03:21.301 --> 00:03:25.353
Seven and five make twelve: ten tenths make one,

43
00:03:25.353 --> 00:03:28.650
so I write two and a small one under the ones.

44
00:03:28.650 --> 00:03:31.843
One and the new one make two.

45
00:03:31.843 --> 00:03:35.241
The answer is two point two six.

46
00:03:37.141 --> 00:03:39.231
Here is a worked example.

47
00:03:39.231 --> 00:03:45.264
Calculate two pounds forty-eight plus one pound thirty-five.

48
00:03:46.514 --> 00:03:49.718
One pence: eight plus five equals thirteen.

49
00:03:49.718 --> 00:03:55.268
Ten one pence coins make ten pence: write three and a small one under the ten pence.

50
00:03:55.268 --> 00:03:59.122
Ten pence: four plus three plus one equals eight.

51
00:03:59.122 --> 00:04:01.827
Pounds: two plus one equals three.

52
00:04:01.827 --> 00:04:03.836
Three pounds eighty-three.

53
00:04:03.836 --> 00:04:05.322
Pause the video.

54
00:04:05.322 --> 00:04:08.041
Try the next one in your booklet.

55
00:04:17.341 --> 00:04:19.129
Now let's try a question together.

56
00:04:19.129 --> 00:04:23.227
Calculate one pound eighty-three plus two pounds forty-one.

57
00:04:23.227 --> 00:04:26.050
Pause the video and have a go.

58
00:04:34.700 --> 00:04:37.614
One pence: three plus one equals four.

59
00:04:37.614 --> 00:04:41.039
Ten pence: eight plus four equals twelve.

60
00:04:41.039 --> 00:04:46.438
Ten ten pence coins make one pound: write two and a small one under the pounds.

61
00:04:46.438 --> 00:04:50.594
Pounds: one plus two plus one equals four.

62
00:04:50.594 --> 00:04:52.800
Four pounds twenty-four.

63
00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:55.269
Well done if you got it.

64
00:04:57.169 --> 00:04:58.957
Now try it in your booklet.

65
00:04:58.957 --> 00:05:01.859
Remember: line up the decimal points.

66
00:05:01.859 --> 00:05:06.585
Add the one pence coins first, then the ten pence coins, then the pounds.

67
00:05:06.585 --> 00:05:09.545
Ten one pence coins make ten pence.

68
00:05:09.545 --> 00:05:12.541
Ten ten pence coins make one pound.

69
00:05:12.541 --> 00:05:14.023
Good luck.
